## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical integration of real-time data streams, memoization strategies, and optimistic UI patterns within multi-tenant architectures.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant useSyncExternalStore streams
- Memoized selectors keyed by (tenantId, notificationId)
- React.memo for individual notification items
- react-window virtualization for performance
- Optimistic UI updates with rollback capability
- Cleanup on tenant switch and reconnection handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Per-tenant store wrapper
const createTenantNotificationStore = (tenantId) => {
  const subscribers = new Set();
  let notifications = [];

  return {
    subscribe: (callback) => {
      subscribers.add(callback);
      return () => subscribers.delete(callback);
    },
    getSnapshot: () => notifications,
    getServerSnapshot: () => [],
  };
};

// Memoized selector
const createNotificationSelector = (tenantId, notificationId) => {
  return createSelector(
    [selectNotificationsByTenant(tenantId)],
    (notifications) => notifications.find(n => n.id === notificationId)
  );
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests mastery of closures, Promise coordination, and cache invalidation patterns in JavaScript without DOM dependencies.

## Key Concepts
- Closures for maintaining per-URL cache state
- Promise deduplication for concurrent in-flight requests
- Stale-while-revalidate caching strategy
- Race condition prevention and cache lifecycle management

## Code Example
```javascript
function makeFetcher() {
  const cache = new Map();
  return {
    fetchMemo: (url, ttlMs) => {
      const getEntry = () => cache.get(url) || { value: null, ts: 0, inFlight: null };
      const fetchAndUpdate = async () => {
        try {
          const response = await fetch(url);
          const data = await response.json();
          cache.set(url, { value: data, ts: Date.now(), inFlight: null });
          return data;
        } catch (error) {
          const entry = getEntry();
          entry.inFlight = null;
          throw error;
        }
      };

      return {
        get: async () => {
          const entry = getEntry();
          const now = Date.now();
          const isFresh = entry.value && (now - entry.ts) < ttlMs;

          if (isFresh) return entry.value;

          if (entry.inFlight) {
            await entry.inFlight;
            return getEntry().value;
          }

          if (entry.value) {
            entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
            return entry.value;
          }

          entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
          return await entry.inFlight;
        },
        invalidate: () => cache.delete(url)
      };
    }
  };
}
```

## Demonstration
```javascript
const fetcher = makeFetcher();

// Set up two URLs with different TTLs
const api1 = fetcher.fetchMemo('https://api.example.com/data1', 5000);
const api2 = fetcher.fetchMemo('https://api.example.com/data2', 10000);

// Concurrent callers will observe stale data immediately while fresh data loads in background
```

