## Why This Is Asked

Tests beginner ability to reason about Lighthouse issues, bundle splitting, and lazy-loading with a realistic small app.

## Key Concepts

- Code splitting with dynamic imports
- Lazy-loading assets/images
- Visibility gate using IntersectionObserver
- Lighthouse CI validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// lazy load heavy widget
const Heavy = React.lazy(() => import('./HeavyWidget'));

function Gate() {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  const [show, setShow] = useState(false);
  useEffect(() => {
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => { if (e.isIntersecting) setShow(true); }, {threshold: 0.1});
    if (ref.current) io.observe(ref.current);
    return () => io.disconnect();
  }, []);
  return (
    <div ref={ref}>
      {show ? (
        <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading…</div>}><Heavy/></Suspense>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you translate this plan to a Lighthouse CI workflow?
- How would you handle SSR or non-React pages?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CSS skills: responsive grid, aspect-ratio posters, CSS-only interactivity, and accessibility without JS. The checkbox toggle demonstrates stateful layout changes without scripting, plus progressive enhancement for motion preferences and focus visibility.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid responsive columns and dense placement
- Checkbox-based CSS state toggling
- Grid-area reassignment for reordering (data-id based)
- Accessibility: focus-visible outlines and reduced-motion support

## Code Example
```html
<input type="checkbox" id="sort" aria-label="Sort by popularity" />
<div class="grid">
  <article class="card" data-id="1">
    <div class="poster"></div>
    <h3>Title 1</h3>
    <div class="rating">★★★★☆</div>
  </article>
  <article class="card" data-id="2"></article>
  <article class="card" data-id="3"></article>
</div>
```
```css
.grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap:1rem; }
.card{ background:#111; color:#fff; aspect-ratio:16/9; }
.poster{ width:100%; height:0; padding-bottom:56.25%; background:#333; }
#sort:checked ~ .grid .card[data-id="1"]{ grid-column:2; grid-row:1; }
#sort:checked ~ .grid .card[data-id="2"]{ grid-column:3; grid-row:1; }
#sort:checked ~ .grid .card[data-id="3"]{ grid-column:4; grid-row:1; }
.card{ animation: fadeIn .4s ease both; animation-delay: calc(var(--d,0)*.05s); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){ .card{ animation: none; } }
:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid #fff; outline-offset:2px; }
@media (max-width: 1024px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 640px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@keyframes fadeIn{ from{ opacity:.0; transform: translateY(6px);} to{ opacity:1; transform:none;} }
```

